From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:45:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(library): Kiro CLI gets the Library's skills, MCP servers
 and instructions (#4769)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The library's targets are agent.All plus apps, and apps held Claude
Desktop alone: Kiro CLI, which magpie wires no model into and the Agents
page rightly leaves alone, could be given none of the three, and a user
of it copied skills, servers and instructions into ~/.kiro by hand
(#4769, ump45nose).

Kiro CLI is an app now, found by the kiro-cli program alone — PATH,
~/.local/bin, Kiro CLI.app, where provider.KiroExecutable already
looked — never by ~/.kiro, which Kiro Crew and the Kiro IDE keep too. It
reads ~/.kiro/skills, ~/.kiro/settings/mcp.json and
~/.kiro/steering/AGENTS.md, its global steering's AGENTS.md being always
included (kiro.dev/docs). Its mcp.json has a format of its own: entries
of command/args/env or url/headers, no type written, the user's fields
(disabled, autoApprove, disabledTools, oauth) kept, no SSE named — a url
is streamable HTTP, the docs give no way to say SSE — and a ${NAME} in
headers or env passed through, Kiro expanding those its Mcp Approved Env
Vars approves.

What a kiro-cli in a WSL distro is given, and a project's .kiro, stays
out: apps are this machine's, and per-tool off stays the user's.

Run: go test -tags nogui ./internal/library (ok; TestKiroCLITarget,
TestKiroCLINotByItsFolder and TestKiroMCP new); go vet (darwin, linux,
windows; nogui) and gofmt -l clean on the package; builds for all three
platforms.

